data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b72eccbc37bd82f0","delta":"{\"file_path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"offset\":0,\"limit\":400}"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_END","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b72eccbc37bd82f0"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b72eccbc37bd82f0","messageId":"8c7d7739-9b0e-4087-a2f4-c92889f34b9a","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: ui-plugin-development\\n3: description: Edit project-owned UI Plugin code directly. Ask only before creating a new Plugin identity or first taking over an npm implementation.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator Phase 8 permits writes under project plugins and AppUIModel composition.\\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: # UI Plugin development\\n8: \\n9: This Skill applies to frontend Plugin source/application authoring. The system\\n10: prompt owns general evidence, authorization and completion rules; this Skill\\n11: adds Plugin-specific contracts, not an additional investigation checklist.\\n12: Use the smallest relevant section/reference. A resolved existing target does not\\n13: require a full capability inventory, a new UI-system decision or a nearest\\n14: consumer example before it can be modified.\\n15: \\n16: ## Ownership and admission\\n17: \\n18: Project-owned application props, children, renderers and scoped styles are ordinary\\n19: editable code. Inspect the exact target and any concrete unknown contract; edit\\n20: within the user's request. Public npm component use does not require implementation\\n21: source, extraction or takeover. Existing source-owned Plugin edits keep the current\\n22: ownership, upstream provenance and BASE; do not repeat successful takeover consent.\\n23: Only actual npm implementation edits require `takeover_plugin_source` and its\\n24: explicit user agreement. Canonical Runtime/Context, vendor and generated registries\\n25: remain protected. A thin wrapper's omitted public seam is not justification for\\n26: requiring takeover.\\n27: \\n28: Ask `prepare_ui_plugin_development` once before creating a NEW Plugin identity,\\n29: including wrapping a component as a new Plugin. After confirmation, implement\\n30: its source, supporting modules, existing parent changes, composition and tests.\\n31: The question result is not a per-file allowlist; changed implementation details\\n32: never require the same development question again. Existing Plugin behavior,\\n33: new interactions and project Service files are ordinary edits. Only actual npm\\n34: implementation changes need the separate source-takeover question.\\n35: For new Plugin manifest/placement and delivery details consult only relevant\\n36: sections of [authoring contracts](references/authoring-contracts.md).\\n37: \\n38: ## Local change evidence\\n39: \\n40: Read the existing files that will change, using the actual supplied sourceRoot and\\n41: owner paths. `manifest.json` declares identity/data/capabilities; `definition.ts`\\n42: joins manifest and component; `index.tsx` owns composition/behavior; imported\\n43: stylesheets own presentation. Read a neighboring consumer only for wiring that\\n44: is actually unknown. An npm implementation need not appear in local search.\\n45: \\n46: `inspect_ui_plugin` returns application ownership, public APIs and parent semantic\\n47: composition where declared. sharedModule selects the installed public module;\\n48: use the root module for presentation controls and /contracts for Plugin types.\\n49: Use returned parameterContracts; follow exact parameterQueries only when a required\\n50: signature is missing. `$element` accesses an array/index element, not React props.\\n51: Query concrete exported types for overloaded Hooks, rather than repeatedly\\n52: querying `$return`. Shared-symbol queries return API evidence, not an edit target.\\n53: An unavailable guessed symbol is not a missing capability. Preserve declared\\n54: composition slots when appending controls; replacement props can replace them.\\n55: \\n56: Public types establish invocation shape, not rendered styling. Package-owned\\n57: presentationContract describes raw versus styled components, asset requirements\\n58: and Portal ownership. For a visual defect follow the current owned entry's CSS\\n59: imports and inspect the relevant cascade. Re-querying types cannot establish\\n60: centering. Public overlay composites may own their own Portal and Backdrop;\\n61: respect that composition and retain the existing AgentUIRoot theme container.\\n62: Use the public Trigger/Close/focus APIs. Local dialog state or scoped popup\\n63: positioning does not introduce a Service, Agent action, Runtime replacement or\\n64: source takeover. Verify requested placement, closing and focus in the actual Host.\\n65: \\n66: ## Editing constraints\\n67: \\n68: Freshly read existing edit targets in the current run; old messages/handoff are\\n69: navigation, not current read evidence. `edit_file_from_read` edits a stable range;\\n70: `edit_file` handles small local changes; `mutate_ui_plugin_source` makes one atomic\\n71: Plugin-local transaction with edit/create entries. Re-read and reconcile affected\\n72: files after stale-content errors. Do not hand-edit `registry.generated.ts`, the\\n73: AppUIModel JSON or composition-revision metadata; use their Host tools.\\n74: \\n75: Preserve the target's UI library, enabled capabilities, scope bridge, semantic\\n76: slots and original approval/interrupt/error renderers. New user/screen-reader copy\\n77: uses the unified domain locale namespace with en-US/zh-CN parity; never patch\\n78: vendor for localization. Read locale targets when changing them, not for every\\n79: style edit. Official keys use `useAgentUILocale(namespace)` and `Agent.locales`;\\n80: new business keys belong in the project's shared namespaced messages module,\\n81: selected with the unified `useAgentUILocaleCode()` value. The official Hook is\\n82: not an arbitrary namespace registry. Do not invent per-Plugin i18n hooks, locale\\n83: state or Service abstractions. Follow the packaged Plugin API example.\\n84: \\n85: Styles must be imported and scoped to owned classes/data attributes; no global\\n86: resets, Host ancestor selectors, Runtime/Portal changes or vendor overrides.\\n87: Own box-sizing, min-width and responsive maximum size. Flex/grid children must\\n88: shrink and long text wrap; overlays need bounded dimensions appropriate to the\\n89: actual container. Static heuristics are not visual acceptance. The specialized\\n90: responsive-repair proposal tool is not currently exposed by any Creator tool\\n91: group. For ordinary authorized responsive CSS changes, freshly read the owned\\n92: stylesheet, use the available file-edit tools and validate the current revision.\\n93: If the user explicitly requests the unavailable specialized proposal tool,\\n94: explain that limitation; do not claim to have invoked it.\\n95: \\n96: ## Validation and outcome\\n97: \\n98: Validate source changes at the current revision; include the build for new visual\\n99: Plugins or dependency/style integration as required. Composition changes use fresh\\n100: AppUIModel evidence and normal Host mutation/verification tools. Creation/catalog\\n101: synchronization is not mounting: newly created capabilities must be composed when\\n102: requested, and the final revision validated. Consume checks already performed by\\n103: the Host rather than duplicating them. Respect returned repair limits.\\n104: `validate_creator_changes` synchronizes changed Plugin manifest/definition files\\n105: into `registry.generated.ts` before checking. It is the exposed synchronization\\n106: entry; do not search for an npm script or edit the generated registry. Refresh\\n107: composition after synchronization to discover the new capability before mounting.\\n108: \\n109: Keep static, Runtime and browser evidence distinct. Current tests/types or empty\\n110: Runtime errors do not prove popup geometry, keyboard behavior or focus. Validate\\n111: the requested interactions using available authorized browser/test evidence; report\\n112: missing infrastructure or stale evidence precisely. Do not label incomplete work\\n113: as already satisfied or reopen unrelated discovery when verification is unavailable.\\n114: \",\"hash\":\"1d8ac128dcb7bc83dba4ce277e52f3edd6adef5696c134a403a5eb3a22fbec64\",\"totalLines\":114,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

